{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BorromeanBlochGroupElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BorromeanBlochGroupElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanVolumeCatalan"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.not_borromeanBloch_of_regulator_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.not_borromeanBloch_of_regulator_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L135-L145","doc":"The field **discriminates**: a symbol whose regulator vanishes is not one.\n\nWithout this, satisfiability would be compatible with the class holding of\neverything — the failure mode the `holds : Prop` carrier had. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanBlochGroupElement_example","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanBlochGroupElement_example","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L127-L133","doc":"The field is satisfiable: take `B = ℝ`, `r₂ = id`, `[i] = G`.\n\nA consistency witness only — deliberately a `theorem` and **not** an `instance`, so\nresolution can never discharge the hypothesis for a caller's own `r₂` and `[i]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4Shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4Shadow","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L116-L125","doc":"The `h⁴` shadow: `r₂[𝓑₃] · (−3/4) = −6G`.\n\n`h4` is a parameter and its value is a hypothesis — sourced to the Markov trace of\n`𝓑₃`, not re-derived here. Given it, the product is arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanClass_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanClass_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L104-L114","doc":"The Borromean class is **non-trivial** in `B`.\n\nA non-zero regulator forces a non-zero class, since `r₂` is additive and so sends\n`0` to `0`. The positivity comes from `vol_B3 > 0`, which is proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.regulator_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.regulator_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L92-L102","doc":"**`r₂[𝓑₃] = Vol(𝓑₃) = 8G`** — the block's headline, *derived*.\n\nAdditivity of the regulator on `8·[i]`, then the one assumed value. This is the\nstep the previous `holds : Prop` carrier could not take, because it had nothing to\ntake it from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanClass","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L83-L90","doc":"`[𝓑₃] = 8·[i]`.\n\nThurston: the Borromean complement is two regular ideal octahedra, and each\noctahedron is `4·[i]` in the Bloch group. A **definition**, so the factor `8` is\nstructural rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement.regulator_bloch_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement.regulator_bloch_i","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L81-L81","doc":"`r₂([i]) = G`, Catalan's constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanBlochGroupElement","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.lean#L69-L81","doc":"**Bloch-group input for the Borromean class.**\n\n`B` stands for `B(ℂ)`, `r2` for the Beilinson regulator, and `blochI` for the\nsymbol `[i]` of the fourth root of unity.\n\nThe single field is classical: `r₂([i]) = D(i) = Cl₂(π/2) = G`. Everything the\nblock asserts about `𝓑₃` is derived from it below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:borromean-bloch-group-element","label":"conj:borromean-bloch-group-element","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-bloch-group-element.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}